 a part of </em><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/labyrinth\"><em>labyrinth library</em></a><em>. </em></p><p><em>you can </em><strong><em>listen to an excerpt</em></strong><em> below ~</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/black-box-excerpt\" target=\"_blank\">\n    explore this artifact\n  </a>\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong><em>purpose</em></strong><em> — to shift the focus from seeking transparency to seeking possibility — exploring ways of working with what feels mysterious, opaque, or unknown. to practice bracketing &amp; putting a container around what you cannot understand or control, so that you can experiment with it, encounter it, or endure it.<br /><br /></em><strong><em>guiding question — </em></strong><em>how do you make workable what you don't fully understand, or cannot see?</em></p><p><strong><em>astrological season:</em></strong><em> aries</em></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong>🦋 explore </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/labyrinth\"><strong>labyrinth library</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n ","author":"Kening Zhu","siteTitle":"kening zhu","siteHash":"ef8a94b9fc20c32a4ee7d94ee971337d278e8b2fafe747123e4eb5cea026e84e","entryHash":"98bc7deda2d19e3b35c076fc7edf32016f53e7f414452d282fc7770c991d6058","category":"Sites"}